            "source_entity_instance": "MRI-ESM2-0",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "percentile rank (\u03b7)",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "Three statistical measures are calculated for the annual or seasonal mean of a variable at the arbitrary grid: the fractional range coverages of climate changes by the mini-ensemble (FRCmini) and by a global-warming constraint (FRCGW) and the percentile rank (\u03b7). First, FRCmini is the ratio of the intermodel maximum-minimum difference of future changes in the mini-ensemble to that in the full ensemble with the unit of % (McSweeney et al. 2015). Third, \u03b7 is defined as the rank of future changes of a specific model in the full ensemble with the unit of percentile and averaged for the three scenarios (\u03b7).",
